when you type `*` in the value of the subdomain, it is a wildcard that allows any prefix to be included as a subdomain so you don't have to list them manually


What is the default port for HTTP/HTTPS/SSH? 
  HTTP: 80
  HTTPS:443
  SSH: 22
What does an HTTP status code in the range of 300/400/500 indicate? 
  300-399: Redirection
  400-499: Client errors
  500-599: Server errors
What does the HTTP header content-type allow you to do? 
  Tells the client what type of data is being sent
What does a “Secure cookie”/”Http-only cookie”/”Same-site cookie” do? https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTTP/Cookies 
  Secure cookie: Only sent over HTTPS
  HTTPOnly cookie: Inaccessible to javascript
  SameSite cookie: Controls whether cookies are sent on cross-site requests
