What is the websocket protocol intended to provide? 
  Persistent communication channel between client and server
What do the following acronyms stand for? JSX, JS, AWS, NPM, NVM 
  JSX: Javascript XML
  JS: Javascript
  AWS: Amazon Web Services
  NPM: Node Package Manager
  NVM: Node Version Manager
Assuming an HTML document with a body element. What text content will the following React component generate? The react component will use parameters. 
Given a set of React components that include each other, what will be generated
What does a React component with React.useState do? 
  Declares a state variable inside the component and causes it to re-render when the state changes
What are React Hooks used for? 
  Let functional components use things like state, lifecycle effects, context, ect. without writing classes for them 
What does the State Hook/Context Hook/Ref Hook/Effect Hook/Performance Hook do? https://react.dev/reference/react/hooks 
  State hook: stores mutatable state
  Context hook: Access a value from a React context
  Ref hook: Stores mutatable values that don't re-render, or reference DOM nodes
  Effect hook: Run side effects after render
  Performance hook: memoize expensive computations, memoize functions, smooth UI updates, etc.
Given React Router code, select statements that are true. 
What does the package.json file do? 
  Defines project metadata, lists dependencies, defines scripts, specifies nodes and packages
What does the fetch function do? 
  performs an HTTP request to the back end server, returns a promise, provides in a stream (DOM object, text, blob, etc.)
What does node.js do? 
  Runs javascript outside the browser
What does pm2 do?
  Process manager for node apps
  Auto restarts crashed apps
  handles logs
What does Vite do?
  A fast frontend build tool
  Uses ES solutions, instant dev server, super fast HMR
  Builds optimized production bundles
